/-!
# Orbit partition, link 2 (q=2) — data and kernel checkers: the orbit matrices realize genuine
# normalizer conjugation

The q=2 (`SmallGroup(3125,69)` / `Coordinate 2`) mirror of
`Twin1/NormLink2Data.lean`. `Generators/Twin2/NormGen.lean` emitted, for each
rep `H = reps r` (echelon basis `B = basisAt2 r`), the conjugation matrices
`normMats r` as `expVec2`s of conjugation by the generators of `normBasis B`
(q=2 group law). This file embeds `normGens r` — the actual `normBasis B`
coordinate elements, in the same outer order as `normMats r` — and provides the
four kernel checkers. Twin note: unlike `normIdxData`, these generators depend
on the q=2 group LAW and are regenerated.

Orientation (as emitted by `conjMatrix` in `Generators/Twin2/NormGen.lean`): row
`i` of `nⱼ`'s matrix is `expVec2 B (conjC 2 (invC 2 nⱼ) gᵢ) = expVec2_B (nⱼ⁻¹ gᵢ nⱼ)`.
-/

namespace LeanDring.P5Presentation.Q2

open Fin.NatCast

set_option maxRecDepth 100000

